### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is false. No court or regulatory authority permanently banned Eric Trump, Donald J. Trump Jr., or Ivanka Trump from operating a charity. The New York Supreme Court’s final resolution in November 2019 did not impose such a ban, but instead required them to undergo board training on fiduciary responsibilities ([Snopes](https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/trump-steal-kids-cancer-charity/)). The New York Attorney General’s request for a one-year ban was never granted ([PolitiFact](https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2019/oct/24/facebook-posts/trump-family-disallowed-operating-charities-new-yo/)). Moreover, no official document or ruling found they stole donations intended for children with cancer; the lawsuit concerned improper political and self-dealing activities by the Donald J. Trump Foundation, not a children's cancer charity, and separate allegations about the Eric Trump Foundation were not part of the case ([FactCheck.org](https://www.factcheck.org/2019/12/social-posts-distort-facts-on-trump-charities/)).